x535 text "primer"
x536 puts x534 x535
x537 call open x536 11
x538 write x537 2
x539 text "The primer"
x540 puts x538 x539
x541 call close x540 
x542 call open x541 2
x543 write x542 2
x544 text "This is everything a model is told before it writes or edits A0. The sections below say the same thing in full."
x545 puts x543 x544
x546 call close x545 
x547 call open x546 10
x548 write x547 4
x549 write x548 2
x550 text "code wrap"
x551 puts x549 x550
x552 call open x551 4
x553 write x552 2
x554 text "A0: `fn NAME T... -> T`, lines `ID OP ARG...`, `ret ARG`, `end`. Types u32 bool, arrays u32x4, records (u32,bool). Params p0 p1... Args: earlier ID, pN, u32 literal, true, false. Ops exact mod 2^32.\n"
x555 puts x553 x554
x556 write x555 2
x557 text "add sub mul and or xor (bool too) shl shr (count&31) div (b=0: 4294967295) rem (b=0: a) eq ne lt le gt ge (unsigned, -> bool) select c x y\n"
x558 puts x556 x557
x559 write x558 2
x560 text "call F a... | fold F n s a... state=s; i<n: state=F(state,i,a...)\n"
x561 puts x559 x560
x562 write x561 2
x563 text "arr e... | rec e... | get a i (i mod N) | set a i v | at r k | put r k v\n"
x564 puts x562 x563
x565 write x564 2
x566 text "EDIT: reply bare edit lines, e.g. `c add a b` (replaces c or inserts before ret; `c add a b @ x` inserts after x), `-c`, `ret c`, `fn f ...` (adds/replaces a function), `-fn f`.\n"
x567 puts x565 x566
x568 call close x567 
x569 call close x568 
x570 call close x569 
x571 call open x570 13
x572 write x571 4
x573 write x572 1
x574 text "programs"
x575 puts x573 x574
x576 call open x575 11
x577 write x576 2
x578 text "Programs and functions"
x579 puts x577 x578
x580 call close x579 
x581 call open x580 2
x582 write x581 2
x583 text "A program is a list of functions. A function is a header `fn NAME T... -> T`, then one instruction per line `ID OP ARGS`, then `ret ARG` (or `ret OP ARGS`, which names a fresh node), then `end`. Names are lowercase identifiers. Parameters are p0, p1, ... in header order. An argument is an earlier ID in the same function, a parameter, a u32 literal, true, or false. There are no forward references, no recursion, and no nested expressions."
x584 puts x582 x583
x585 call close x584 
x586 call open x585 10
x587 write x586 4
x588 write x587 2
x589 text "code"
x590 puts x588 x589
x591 call open x590 4
x592 call open x591 6
x593 write x592 4
x594 write x593 2
x595 text "cm"
x596 puts x594 x595
x597 write x596 2
x598 text "# clamp p0 into [p1, p2]\n"
x599 puts x597 x598
x600 call close x599 
x601 write x600 2
x602 text "fn clamp u32 u32 u32 -> u32\nlo lt p0 p1\nhi lt p2 p0\na select lo p1 p0\nr select hi p2 a\nret r\nend"
x603 puts x601 x602
x604 call close x603 
x605 call close x604 
x606 call close x605 
x607 call open x606 13
x608 write x607 4
x609 write x608 1
x610 text "types"
x611 puts x609 x610
x612 call open x611 11
x613 write x612 2
x614 text "Types and values"
x615 puts x613 x614
x616 call close x615 
x617 call open x616 2
x618 write x617 2
x619 text "u32 is an exact 32-bit unsigned integer; every arithmetic result wraps modulo 2^32. bool is true or false, never a number. Arrays u32xN and records (T,T,...) are values: get, set, at, and put return a copy, they never alias. io is a linear token, meaning every io value is used exactly once; that is what makes output order checkable."
x620 puts x618 x619
x621 call close x620 
x622 call close x621 
x623 call open x622 13
x624 write x623 4
x625 write x624 1
x626 text "iteration"
x627 puts x625 x626
x628 call open x627 11
x629 write x628 2
x630 text "Iteration"
x631 puts x629 x630
x632 call close x631 
x633 call open x632 2
x634 write x633 2
x635 text "A function body has no loops. Repetition is fold and loop over an earlier function: the step function receives the state, the index, and any extra arguments, and returns the next state. loop adds a predicate function that is checked before each iteration. A literal count is checked against a per-function budget when the program is checked. A variable count is bounded by fuel (a step budget) in the reference interpreter, the plain slow implementation that every target is compared with; compiled targets have no execution budget."
x636 puts x634 x635
x637 call close x636 
x638 call open x637 10
x639 write x638 4
x640 write x639 2
x641 text "code"
x642 puts x640 x641
x643 call open x642 4
x644 call open x643 6
x645 write x644 4
x646 write x645 2
x647 text "cm"
x648 puts x646 x647
x649 write x648 2
x650 text "# sum of squares 0..n-1 with fold; the step is an earlier function\n"
x651 puts x649 x650
x652 call close x651 
x653 write x652 2
x654 text "fn sqstep u32 u32 -> u32\ns mul p1 p1\nr add p0 s\nret r\nend\nfn sumsq -> u32\nr fold sqstep 10 0\nret r\nend"
x655 puts x653 x654
x656 call close x655 
x657 call close x656 
x658 call close x657 
x659 call open x658 13
x660 write x659 4
x661 write x660 1
x662 text "modules"
x663 puts x661 x662
x664 call open x663 11
x665 write x664 2
x666 text "Modules"
x667 puts x665 x666
x668 call close x667 
x669 call open x668 2
x670 write x669 2
x671 text "A file starts with zero or more `use \"path.a0\"` lines, relative to the file. The linker loads every used file once, orders them by dependency, and checks the result as one program with one namespace. Cycles and duplicate function names are rejected, and diagnostics name the file and line."
x672 puts x670 x671
x673 call close x672 
x674 call open x673 10
x675 write x674 4
x676 write x675 2
x677 text "code"
x678 puts x676 x677
x679 call open x678 4
x680 write x679 2
x681 text "use \"ui.a0\"\nuse \"../examples/life.a0\"\nfn page io -> io\na call open p0 5\nb call close a\nret b\nend"
x682 puts x680 x681
x683 call close x682 
x684 call close x683 
x685 call close x684 
ret x685
end

fn sec_iter io -> io
x687 call open p0 13
x688 write x687 4
x689 write x688 1
x690 text "editing"
x691 puts x689 x690
x692 call open x691 11
x693 write x692 2
x694 text "Views and edits"
x695 puts x693 x694
x696 call close x695 
x697 call open x696 2
x698 write x697 2
x699 text "A model never sees a whole file. It asks for a view of one function: the function with a handle line on top (e0), one signature line per callee, and a program handle (g0). The program view is scoped to the target, its transitive callees and its direct callers, so it stays the same size as the program grows. The revision is a short hash of the program text; an edit written against an older revision is rejected rather than applied to code that has moved. A reply is the handle line followed by edits, one per line, as in the quick start."
x700 puts x698 x699
x701 call close x700 
x702 call open x701 10
x703 write x702 4
x704 write x703 2
x705 text "code"
x706 puts x704 x705
x707 call open x706 4
x708 call open x707 6
x709 write x708 4
x710 write x709 2
x711 text "cm"
x712 puts x710 x711
x713 write x712 2
x714 text "# a view of clamp, then a reply that fixes the upper bound\n"
x715 puts x713 x714
x716 call close x715 
x717 write x716 2
x718 text "e0 fn clamp u32 u32 u32 -> u32\nlo lt p0 p1\nhi lt p2 p0\na select lo p1 p0\nr select hi p2 a\nret r\n\n"
x719 puts x717 x718
x720 call open x719 6
x721 write x720 4
x722 write x721 2
x723 text "cm"
x724 puts x722 x723
x725 write x724 2
x726 text "# reply\n"
x727 puts x725 x726
x728 call close x727 
x729 write x728 2
x730 text "e0\nhi lt p2 a\nr select hi p2 a"
x731 puts x729 x730
x732 call close x731 
x733 call close x732 
x734 call close x733 
x735 call open x734 13
x736 write x735 4
x737 write x736 1
x738 text "diagnostics"
x739 puts x737 x738
x740 call open x739 11
x741 write x740 2
x742 text "Diagnostics"
x743 puts x741 x742
x744 call close x743 
x745 call open x744 2
x746 write x745 2
x747 text "Every rejection carries a stable code (parse, type, structure, handle, revision, limit), what was expected, what was seen, and the one fix that resolves it. The compiler never guesses: an ambiguous reply is rejected with the fix, not applied approximately."
x748 puts x746 x747
x749 call close x748 
x750 call close x749 
ret x750
end

